      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 104, fountain grass. The row's name Pennisetum alopecuroides is a synonym; NC State uses Cenchrus alopecuroides, RHS still files it under Pennisetum alopecuroides and says Cenchrus is the synonym; the entry key follows NC State and the other name is a synonym. Care: NC State and RHS agree on full sun, well-drained soil and cutting back in late winter. Two care sources only (the Missouri BG search returned no page for it). Size: RHS 1 to 1.5 m by 1 to 1.5 m, NC State 60 to 180 cm by 60 to 120 cm; 120 by 120 cm is a mapping. Hardiness H3 is the RHS rating but RHS also says it may need winter protection in colder areas, and NC State gives zone 6 to 9, so treat it as a lower bound (confidence from_knowledge_verify). Placement in pots is not stated by either page: guess, from the row. NC State warns it self-seeds and has escaped gardens; sterile cultivars (Cayenne, Hush Puppy, Praline) are listed. Toxicity: no page read states any, no ASPCA page, so people and pets are unknown. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
